  "problem_statement": "fix(llm): retry OpenRouter gateway 5xx errors instead of giving up in 1 try\n\nHit live: the vision profile's free OpenRouter model returned\n{'message': 'Upstream idle timeout exceeded', 'code': 504} -- an HTTP 200\nwith an embedded error body, which langchain_openai surfaces as a bare\nValueError rather than an openai.*Error subclass. _is_transient() only\nrecognized the openai exception types, so this fell through to \"not\ntransient\" and the run gave up after one attempt despite LLM_MAX_RETRIES=5\nbeing configured. Now ValueError({'code': <5xx or 429>, ...}) is classified\ntransient too, so the existing backoff loop actually runs. Verified the\nretry recovers via a fake LLM that raises this error twice then succeeds.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
